# Optional overrides. The app uses ESPN's public, unauthenticated endpoints by default.
# No API key is required for scores or the highlights strip.

# Host only — sport/league path is appended from the SportLeague registry
# (`/apis/site/v2/sports/{sport}/{league}`). A leftover full CFB path is stripped
# to the origin so Phase 0 can parameterize other leagues later.
# ESPN_WEB_BASE=https://site.web.api.espn.com
# ESPN_SITE_BASE=https://site.api.espn.com

# Optional. Highlights default to public YouTube channel RSS (no key).
# Set this only if you want YouTube Data API search mixed into the strip.
# When RSS is down, the strip shows a labeled empty — never fake video ids or scores.
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# Reserved for a later third-party odds feed. Deep Dive v0 does not call a
# paid odds API even if this key is present. Prop cards still render;
# edge_vs_market stays null. ESPN pickcenter (when published) is Evidence only.
# ODDS_API_KEY=

# Optional Google Gemini key for Stat Oracle historical / off-feed answers.
# Any ONE of these names works (first match wins). This is a Gemini API key
# from Google AI Studio — not a Custom Search Engine (CSE) id, and not CSE cx=.
# When set, /oracle uses Gemini with Google Search grounding for questions
# that are not on the current ESPN slice (e.g. "Who won the 1974 NBA Finals?").
# Without a key, Oracle stays ESPN-slice only (NOT ON THIS FEED).
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional model override (defaults to gemini-2.5-flash, then gemini-2.0-flash).
# GEMINI_MODEL=

# Optional free CollegeFootballData Bearer token.
# https://collegefootballdata.com — request a key, then:
# CFBD_API_KEY=
# Without it, Deep Dive and Stat Oracle stay ESPN-only and label CFBD as not configured.

# Optional folder of Deep Lore / Post-Game X-Ray files for /research.
# Defaults to repo-local research/ plus public/research/ (DELL drop folder).
# Lab box example: RESEARCH_DIR=/workspace/harmon-line-lab
# RESEARCH_DIR=
